# general
.*
_*

# …but Python packages need their underscore-prefixed modules committed,
# otherwise hatchling (which honours VCS ignore files) drops them from wheels.
#
# Un-ignore the source TREES, not one module name at a time. The allowlist
# that used to live here was a list of names someone had remembered to add,
# and `_api.py` and `_transport.py` — the whole Python client — were silently
# left out of a commit because nobody had. `pixi run xtask check-sources`
# fails the gate if this ever stops covering a source file again.
!__init__.py
!__init__.pyi
!__main__.py
!py-packages/*/python/**/_*.py
!py-packages/*/python/**/_*.pyi
!py-packages/*/src/**/_*.py
!py-packages/*/src/**/_*.pyi
!py-packages/*/tests/**/_*.py
!ts-packages/*/src/**/_*.ts
!ts-packages/*/src/**/_*.js
!ts-packages/*/tests/**/_*.ts
!ts-packages/*/tests/**/_*.js
!crates/*/src/**/_*.rs
!crates/*/tests/**/_*.rs

# git / github
!.git*

# devcontainer (the general .* rule would otherwise hide it)
!.devcontainer/

# knowledge bundle
!.knowledge/

# agent skills and conventional-release config
!.agents/
!.versionrc

# pixi
!.pixi/config.toml
# The sandbox publish plan is `pixi-sandbox.toml` (no leading dot as of
# pixi-sandbox v0.4.0, which made the dotted name a legacy fallback). The
# general `.*` rule above therefore no longer hides it and needs no un-ignore.

# cargo
/target
!.cargo
# Local pixi-sandbox vendor redirect (machine-local); never commit it —
# CI must resolve crates from crates.io.
.cargo/config.toml

# cpp
!.clang*
compile_commands.json
symbology-style.db

# pixi-sandbox
.pixi-sandbox/
dist/

# turbo (local task cache)
.turbo/

# docs app (Bun / Astro)
docs/node_modules/
# The Bun workspace at the root owns JS resolution and its root bun.lock is the
# single lockfile. A root npm lock, or a member lock under ts-packages/, is a
# mistake: two lockfiles for one dependency graph resolve differently.
/package-lock.json
ts-packages/*/package-lock.json
docs/package-lock.json
docs/dist/
docs/.astro/

# bun / node / napi — every JS package lives in ts-packages/
node_modules/
ts-packages/*/dist/
# the compiled addon napi build drops next to the package.json
ts-packages/qgis-node/*.node
ts-packages/qgis-node/npm/*/bin/

# python — wheels and editable installs built from py-packages/<name>
py-packages/*/*.egg-info/
py-packages/*/.pytest_cache/
gate.log
